                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238313124",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198163310887",
                            "num_reviews": 17,
                            "playtime_forever": 749,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 749,
                            "last_played": 1792352136
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I finished the first season of Telltale's Batman earlier this year for the first time, and finally got round to checking out Season 2 last week.\r\n\r\nOut of all of their games. this is the only Telltale series in which I went in completely blind knowing nothing prior, and I had a great time - as an absolute Batman fanatic/someone who's played through the Arkham games religiously on the Xbox 360 I don't know why it took me so long to check out Telltale's iteration of the Caped Crusader and boy was I missing out.\r\n\r\nThe quick time combat events/combos are so insanely satisfying to hit, the story actually felt like it held so much weight bearing my choices, and the voice acting is just top notch especially from actor Anthony Ingruber who plays \"John Doe\"/ Joker in honestly one of the best portrayals I've ever seen across Batman media. While I very much enjoyed the first season, the second season won me over and is just better in alot of ways. If you're a fan of Batman and decision based games that'll make you so procrastinated you'll have to pause the game (like I did) then I can't recommend this series enough.\r\n\r\n9/10",
